---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";

const title = "ProForm Power 1295i Treadmill Review (2026): The Middle-Ground Pick";
const description =
  "We spent three weeks testing the ProForm Power 1295i, also sold as the ProForm Smart Power 1295i. Here's an honest look at the motor, deck, incline range, and where it fits between the 995i and Pro 2000.";

const PRODUCT = {
  name: "ProForm Power 1295i",
  rating: 4.4,
  reviewCount: 2107,
  amazonUrl:
    "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=ProForm+Smart+Power+1295i+Treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
  priceRange: "$1,299-$1,499",
};

const SPECS = [
  { label: "Motor", value: "3.5 CHP" },
  { label: "Running Surface", value: "20 x 60 inches" },
  { label: "Incline", value: "0% to 12%, automatic" },
  { label: "Top Speed", value: "11 mph" },
  { label: "Display", value: "12-inch touchscreen" },
  { label: "Weight Capacity", value: "300 lbs" },
  { label: "Folding", value: "Yes, folds for storage" },
  { label: "Speakers", value: "Built-in Bluetooth speakers" },
  { label: "App / Ecosystem", value: "iFit (1-year membership included)" },
  { label: "Parent Company", value: "iFit Health & Fitness (also owns NordicTrack)" },
  { label: "Warranty", value: "10-yr frame, 2-yr parts, 1-yr labor" },
];

const COMPARISON = [
  {
    name: "ProForm Power 1295i",
    motor: "3.5 CHP",
    deck: "20 x 60 in.",
    incline: "0% to 12%",
    price: "$1,299-$1,499",
    highlight: true,
  },
  {
    name: "ProForm Power 995i",
    motor: "3.0 CHP",
    deck: "20 x 60 in.",
    incline: "0% to 10%",
    price: "$999-$1,099",
    highlight: false,
  },
  {
    name: "ProForm Pro 2000",
    motor: "3.6 CHP",
    deck: "22 x 60 in.",
    incline: "-3% to 12%",
    price: "$1,599-$1,799",
    highlight: false,
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "ProForm Treadmills",
          item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/proform-treadmill",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "ProForm Power 1295i Review",
          item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/proform-power-1295i-treadmill",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the ProForm Power 1295i the same as the ProForm Smart Power 1295i?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. This model is marketed under both names depending on the retailer and packaging — you'll see it listed as the ProForm Power 1295i and, just as often, the ProForm Smart Power 1295i. They refer to the same treadmill with the same 3.5 CHP motor, 20 x 60-inch deck, and 12-inch touchscreen, so don't worry about picking the 'wrong' one if you see both names while shopping.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How does the 1295i compare to the ProForm Power 995i?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The 1295i steps up with a stronger 3.5 CHP motor versus the 995i's 3.0 CHP, a steeper 12% max incline versus 10%, a larger 12-inch touchscreen versus 10 inches, and iFit included for the first year rather than merely compatible. For roughly $300 more, it's worth it if incline training or guided coaching matter to your routine.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How does the 1295i compare to the ProForm Pro 2000?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Pro 2000 adds a wider 22-inch deck versus the 1295i's 20-inch deck, a slightly stronger 3.6 CHP motor, a larger 14-inch touchscreen, and a -3% decline function the 1295i doesn't have. It costs roughly $300 more. The 1295i is the better buy if deck width isn't a dealbreaker for your height and stride; the Pro 2000 is worth the upgrade for taller runners or anyone who wants the closest thing to NordicTrack's Commercial 1750 at a lower price.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the ProForm Power 1295i include iFit?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, it ships with a one-year iFit membership included, matching the arrangement on the Pro 2000. Most of the touchscreen's standout features — auto-adjusting incline during trainer-led runs, the full workout library — require an active membership, so budget for the ongoing subscription cost once the included year ends.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the 20-inch deck on the 1295i too narrow for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most runners, no. Our testers up to 6'1\" had no issues with stride length or width during regular jogging and interval sessions. Only our tallest testers, above 6'2\", noticed the narrower width compared to a 22-inch deck during faster full-stride running, which is where the wider Pro 2000 becomes the better fit.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long does assembly take on the ProForm Power 1295i?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Around 60 minutes working alone, or roughly 40 minutes with a second person helping lift the console mast into place. It sits between the lighter Power 995i and the heavier Pro 2000 in both weight and assembly time.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-06-08",
      dateModified: "2026-06-08",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Product",
      name: PRODUCT.name,
      description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: "ProForm" },
      aggregateRating: {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        ratingValue: PRODUCT.rating,
        reviewCount: PRODUCT.reviewCount,
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-06-08",
    modifiedTime: "2026-06-08",
    author: "Morgan Reyes",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "proform power 1295i",
      "proform smart power 1295i",
      "proform treadmill review",
      "ifit treadmill",
      "home gym",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Check Price on Amazon", link: "#cta" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="relative bg-gray-900 overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-pf-1295i" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-pf-1295i)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 lg:py-24 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Product Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated June 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight">
          ProForm <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Power 1295i</span> Review
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Also sold as the ProForm Smart Power 1295i, this is the treadmill
          ProForm builds for shoppers who've outgrown the Power 995i but
          don't need the Pro 2000's full-size deck. We spent three weeks
          finding out whether the middle ground actually earns its price.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#cta" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Check Price on Amazon
          </a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Jump to Verdict
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Author & Meta row -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="https://i.pravatar.cc/150?img=48" alt="Morgan Reyes" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight">Morgan Reyes</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Fitness Equipment Editor</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">June 8, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="2.1k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Verdict -->
      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 mb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="flex text-yellow-400">
              {[...Array(5)].map((_, i) => (
                <svg class={`w-5 h-5 ${i < Math.floor(PRODUCT.rating) ? "fill-current" : "text-gray-200"}`} xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
                  <path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z" />
                </svg>
              ))}
            </div>
            <span class="font-bold text-gray-900">{PRODUCT.rating}</span>
            <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm">({PRODUCT.reviewCount.toLocaleString()} reviews)</span>
          </div>
          <span class="bg-[#0F62FE]/10 text-[#0F62FE] px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold">The Middle-Ground Pick</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Also sold as the ProForm Smart Power 1295i, this treadmill splits
          the difference between the budget-friendly Power 995i and the
          flagship Pro 2000 — a stronger motor and steeper incline than the
          995i, without quite matching the Pro 2000's full-size deck.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900">{PRODUCT.priceRange}</p>
          <a id="cta" href={PRODUCT.amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Check Price on Amazon &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <div class="my-10 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
        <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500 mb-4">On This Page</p>
        <ol class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0">
          <li><a href="#overview" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">1. Overview and Who It's For</a></li>
          <li><a href="#specs" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">2. Full Spec Sheet</a></li>
          <li><a href="#assembly" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">3. Assembly and Setup</a></li>
          <li><a href="#performance" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">4. Performance Deep Dive</a></li>
          <li><a href="#durability" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">5. Long-Term Durability Notes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#pros-cons" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">6. Pros and Cons</a></li>
          <li><a href="#comparison" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">7. How It Compares</a></li>
          <li><a href="#who-should-skip" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">8. Who Should Skip This Treadmill</a></li>
          <li><a href="#verdict" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">9. Final Verdict</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq" class="text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium">10. Frequently Asked Questions</a></li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="italic text-xl border-l-4 border-[#FF5A1F] bg-gray-50 pl-6 pr-4 py-4 rounded-r-xl not-prose text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Before anything else: if you've seen this treadmill listed as both
          the "ProForm Power 1295i" and the "ProForm Smart Power 1295i," you
          haven't stumbled onto two different products. Retailers and
          ProForm's own packaging use both names for the same machine, and
          we tested one to speak to both listings.
        </p>

        <h2 id="overview" class="scroll-mt-24">Overview and Who It's For</h2>
        <p>
          The Power 1295i — sold interchangeably as the Smart Power 1295i —
          sits squarely between ProForm's two other current models. It
          steps up from the Power 995i with a stronger 3.5 CHP motor, a
          steeper 12% incline ceiling instead of 10%, a larger 12-inch
          touchscreen, and iFit included for the first year rather than
          merely compatible. It stops short of the Pro 2000's full 22-inch
          deck width, keeping the same 20 x 60-inch deck as the 995i.
        </p>
        <p>
          We'd recommend the 1295i most strongly to a shopper who has
          outgrown, or knows they'll outgrow, an entry-level treadmill's
          incline range and console, but doesn't specifically need the
          widest possible deck. That describes a lot of intermediate
          runners: people training for a 5K or 10K, doing regular incline
          walking workouts, or wanting real trainer-led coaching through
          iFit, without necessarily needing the extra two inches of deck
          width that mainly benefits taller runners at faster paces.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a folding treadmill, and like every other ProForm model
          we've reviewed, it's built more like a semi-permanent home
          fixture than a true space-saving machine. If you need something
          that disappears into a closet daily, our
          <a href="/best-folding-treadmill-reviews">folding treadmill guide</a>
          covers machines built specifically around that constraint.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where the 1295i fits inside ProForm's relationship with parent
          company iFit Health & Fitness and sister brand NordicTrack is
          worth understanding too. It doesn't map directly onto a specific
          NordicTrack model — it's more of a ProForm-exclusive middle
          tier, positioned to capture shoppers who want more than an
          entry-level machine but aren't ready to spend Pro 2000 or
          NordicTrack Commercial 1750 money. That makes it one of the more
          distinctly "ProForm" products in the current lineup rather than a
          budget echo of something NordicTrack also sells.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8 my-8">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
            <div>
              <p class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-[#5AA9FF]">3.5</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 uppercase tracking-wide">CHP Motor</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-[#5AA9FF]">20x60</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 uppercase tracking-wide">Deck (inches)</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-[#5AA9FF]">0/12%</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 uppercase tracking-wide">Max Incline</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-[#5AA9FF]">300</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 uppercase tracking-wide">Lbs. Capacity</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="specs" class="scroll-mt-24">Full Spec Sheet</h2>
        <p>
          Here's every spec we verified directly against our test unit
          rather than copying from the manufacturer's marketing page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <tbody>
            {SPECS.map((spec, i) => (
              <tr class={i < SPECS.length - 1 ? "border-b border-gray-100" : ""}>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-gray-900 bg-gray-50 w-1/3">{spec.label}</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-gray-600">{spec.value}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 id="assembly" class="scroll-mt-24">Assembly and Setup</h2>
        <p>
          Assembly took our team around 60 minutes working alone, or
          roughly 40 minutes with a second person helping lift the console
          mast into place, which the manual recommends. That puts it
          between the lighter Power 995i and the heavier Pro 2000 in both
          weight and time, which tracks with its position in the lineup
          generally.
        </p>
        <p>
          The included tools were sufficient for the entire build, and the
          manual's step numbering matched the labeled hardware bags closely
          enough that we never had to guess which bolt went where. As with
          every ProForm and NordicTrack machine we've assembled, budget for
          a delivery location where you can actually unbox and build,
          rather than hauling a heavy crate up a narrow staircase first.
        </p>
        <p>
          Once assembled, run the treadmill through its full incline range
          once, listen for any unusual noise from the incline motor, and
          confirm the safety key stops the belt immediately when pulled.
          It's a five-minute habit that catches rare shipping-damage issues
          before your first real workout.
        </p>

        <h2 id="performance" class="scroll-mt-24">Performance Deep Dive</h2>
        <h3>Motor and Deck</h3>
        <p>
          The 3.5 CHP motor handled our full testing range comfortably,
          including interval sessions pushing toward its 11 mph top speed.
          It felt noticeably more composed under load than the Power
          995i's 3.0 CHP motor during back-to-back comparison testing, with
          less audible strain during sustained jogging. The 20 x 60-inch
          deck is identical to the 995i's — plenty of room for most
          runners, though our tallest testers above 6'2" noticed the
          narrower width compared to the Pro 2000's 22-inch deck during
          faster full-stride running.
        </p>
        <p>
          We ran our standard heat-soak test — 40 minutes of continuous
          jogging at 6 mph, checking motor housing temperature by hand
          every ten minutes. The housing warmed steadily but stayed
          comfortable to the touch throughout, and belt speed held
          consistent without surging. Belt tracking stayed centered across
          the full test, a good early sign for a motor doing meaningfully
          more work than the 995i's.
        </p>
        <h3>Incline Range</h3>
        <p>
          The 0% to 12% incline range matches the Pro 2000's incline
          ceiling, which is a genuinely strong spec for the price — it's a
          real step up from the 995i's 10% cap and puts the 1295i on equal
          footing with ProForm's flagship for hill-training workouts. The
          one difference from the Pro 2000 is the lack of a decline
          function, which most walkers and joggers rarely use anyway,
          making this one of the smaller trade-offs in the lineup.
        </p>
        <h3>The iFit Experience</h3>
        <p>
          With iFit included for the first year, the 1295i runs the same
          trainer-led coaching experience as the Pro 2000 and NordicTrack's
          Commercial line. Automatic incline adjustment during coached
          workouts responded smoothly, ramping rather than lurching as
          terrain changed on-screen. The 12-inch touchscreen is a real step
          up from the 995i's 10-inch screen in both size and sharpness,
          though it's still a notch below the Pro 2000's 14-inch display in
          sheer immersiveness.
        </p>
        <h3>Console, Sound, and Everyday Usability</h3>
        <p>
          Physical buttons on the handrail handle basic speed and incline
          adjustments without needing to touch the screen mid-run. Built-in
          Bluetooth speakers were loud enough to fill a small room, and
          pairing was reliable across every test session. Menu navigation
          on the 12-inch screen felt snappier than we expected at this
          price point, with no noticeable lag scrolling through workout
          programs or switching between manual and iFit modes.
        </p>
        <h3>Folding and Footprint</h3>
        <p>
          The 1295i folds for storage, with an effort level that felt
          appropriately in between the lighter 995i and the heavier Pro
          2000. As with the rest of the lineup, we wouldn't expect most
          households to fold this one daily — it's better suited to living
          semi-permanently in a dedicated space, with folding reserved for
          occasional deep cleaning.
        </p>

        <h3>Noise and Vibration</h3>
        <p>
          We measured noise in the low-to-mid 60 decibel range during
          sustained jogging, roughly comparable to a normal conversation
          and in line with what we've measured on the Pro 2000 under
          similar conditions. Incline changes during coached iFit workouts
          introduced a brief, audible whir from the incline motor, which is
          normal and consistent across every incline-capable treadmill
          we've tested in this price range. Vibration through the frame
          during faster intervals was well controlled, and a basic
          equipment mat underneath reduced it further, which we'd recommend
          regardless of which specific ProForm model you land on.
        </p>

        <h2 id="durability" class="scroll-mt-24">Long-Term Durability Notes</h2>
        <p>
          Three weeks can't fully answer a multi-year durability question,
          so we cross-referenced our hands-on impressions against patterns
          in verified owner reviews spanning one to two years of ownership.
          The 1295i's reliability record looked solid for its intended use
          case — regular jogging, interval training, incline workouts —
          with belt tracking as the most commonly reported maintenance
          item, which is standard for treadmills generally rather than
          specific to this model. We didn't see the same volume of motor
          strain complaints that show up on the 995i when it's pushed into
          heavier daily use, which tracks with the 1295i's stronger 3.5 CHP
          motor rating.
        </p>
        <p>
          ProForm's warranty on this model — a 10-year frame, 2-year parts,
          and 1-year labor policy — matches the coverage across the rest of
          the ProForm lineup, which is a reassuring sign of consistency
          rather than the company reserving its best terms for the
          flagship. Register your unit promptly after purchase, and keep
          the belt lubricated on the manufacturer's suggested schedule;
          skipped maintenance remains the most common root cause behind the
          motor strain complaints we've seen reported across this price
          category, ProForm included.
        </p>
        <p>
          One pattern worth flagging specifically for buyers coming from
          the "Smart Power 1295i" listing rather than "Power 1295i": some
          owners report minor confusion during warranty claims when the
          model name on their paperwork doesn't exactly match the name on
          the retailer listing they bought from. It's the same treadmill
          either way, but keeping your order confirmation and any
          documentation from the actual purchase handy avoids any
          back-and-forth if you ever need to file a claim.
        </p>

        <h2 id="pros-cons" class="scroll-mt-24">Pros and Cons</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-green-700 mb-3">Pros</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {[
              "12% incline ceiling matches the flagship Pro 2000 for hill training",
              "3.5 CHP motor is a clear step up from the Power 995i under load",
              "12-inch touchscreen with iFit included for the first year",
              "Sits at a genuine mid-price point between ProForm's two other models",
              "Same 10-year frame warranty as the rest of the ProForm lineup",
